cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the archived aggregate results, please cite the manuscript and this release."
title: "Intraoperative hypotension and acute kidney injury across three perioperative databases (MOVER, VitalDB and INSPIRE)"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, locked analysis contract and aggregate expected results for a
  multi-database study of intraoperative hypotension and 48-hour
  creatinine-defined acute kidney injury. The locked primary analysis (v1.0)
  harmonised the MOVER (United States) and VitalDB (South Korea) databases to
  test whether concentrating 20 minutes of hypotension into one episode carries
  greater risk than distributing the same duration across four episodes. The
  v2.x post hoc analyses add a third cohort (INSPIRE, charted approximately
  every 5 minutes), a resampling control in which the two waveform cohorts were
  reduced to 5-minute sampling, absolute-risk estimates standardized to each
  cohort, and a spline description of the shape of the association. Version
  2.0.1 corrects an outcome-encoding error in 2.0.0 that inverted the odds
  ratios for the resampled and INSPIRE cohorts. No patient-level data are
  included.
